{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261005_112926_3ece21", "exit_code": 0, "text": "No source recovered in my bounded cis audit supplies that combined contrast: endogenous TEAD-site mutation × YAP/TAZ, stiffness or NRG perturbation, with promoter-specific nascent initiation and separation from active EGR2/state effects.\n\nThe most useful locators are:\n\n1. Pantera thesis, Chapter 1, printed p14 / PDF p22.\n   This explicitly describes TEAD-site mutations in luciferase constructs containing the B, C or intronic enhancer sequences, separately from Tead1 knockdown in primary rat/S16 cells and in-vivo YAP/TAZ loss. Those motif mutations are reporter experiments—not endogenous TEAD-site edits. It cites Lopez-Anido et al. 2016, PMC5181599, DOI10.1093/hmg/ddw158.\n\n2. Pantera thesis, Chapter 2, printed pp62–63 / PDF pp70–71.\n   The discussion connects TEAD1 occupancy at B/C and reported P1 bias to the whole-super-enhancer deletion results. The underlying rat S16-derived clone experiment measures steady-state first-exon RNA. It does not isolate TEAD-motif necessity during an extrinsic-input response.\n\n3. PMC7145652, Figure 1D and Methods.\n   This is a nearby endogenous-human editing × NRG1/dbcAMP context, but the edited sequence is the P1 TATA box, not a TEAD site. The seven-day differentiation endpoint is total PMP22 RT-qPCR, not promoter-specific initiation.\n\nImportant coverage limit: my PMC5181599 assessment used its recovered primary abstract and the thesis account, not a complete final-paper methods audit. Your separate audit can therefore strengthen or overturn this bounded negative eligibility result.\n\nThe existing source-located matrix remains:\nartifact_c29f4ea4bba4c049e5387ad507ab14d3a25699b80017b0896bcca3bb62114f48\n\nI recorded these locators and the limitation in LABBOOK and verified the completed snapshot. No reanalysis or raw processing was performed.", "tokens": {"input": 25315, "output": 3617, "total": 842500, "cache_read": 813568, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 132900, "timestamp": 1791228267007}
